# A board's report never takes the place of the shape editor's own message (#303's behaviour
# review, round 2, M3). With a triangle drawn and not saved, q warns that the changes aren't
# saved; another program then writes a board with a card left out, and its report waits
# until the next key has cleared the warning.
size 140x44
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
wait-for example-workspace 35 notes
keys w
wait-for whiteboards · type to filter · ⏎ open · Esc back
type Sketches
keys enter
wait-for whiteboard Sketches · 0 cards
keys S
wait-for shape editor · type to filter
keys enter
wait-for shape editor · shape1 (new) · vertices
click 10 34
click 10 64
click 23 79
click 10 34
wait-for closed path of 3 vertices
keys q
wait-for unsaved changes: q again leaves without saving them, ctrl+s saves
write Inbox/Tephra.canvas {"nodes":[{"id":"","type":"text","text":"- [ ] Sweep the roof","x":0,"y":0,"width":200,"height":80}],"edges":[]}\n
wait 2500ms
expect unsaved changes: q again leaves without saving them, ctrl+s saves
expect-not couldn't read
keys v
wait-for canvas couldn't read Inbox/Tephra.canvas: card 1 (id "") is left out
keys q
wait-for unsaved changes: q again leaves without saving them, ctrl+s saves
keys q
wait-for whiteboard Sketches · 0 cards
keys q
wait-for cold-lava workspaces
keys q
exits 0
